In article <sj051fco5pj18@corp.supernews.com>, eva <evaarlene@hotmail.com> writes:
:my question is very simple. iam hooked to my regular phome line now. my 
:phone company is offering digital phone line. ive heard this is much 
:faster. should i switch. is it worth it.

  Please try a telecom-related newsgroup -- while "digital" is in the 
  charter of this group, the topic of "Digital Equipment Corporation"
  (DEC) has nothing to do with ISDN, DSL/ASDL, T1, or other forms of 
  digital signaling.  Please consider the newsgroups comp.dcom.telecom
  and comp.dcom.modems (or other telecommunications-related newsgroup)
  for questions such as this, as you will likely find a rather larger 
  contingent of phone-saavy folks frequenting the more phone-specific 
  or modem-specific newsgroups.

  You will also have to decide how much the communications bandwidth is 
  worth to you, and the answer to this question is largely based on your 
  budget and your local requirements and your preferences and particularly
  the cost structure of your local communications providers -- you can 
  usually acquire as much bandwidth as you are willing to pay for.  The 
  question thus becomes "how much bandwidth are you willing to pay?".

