Back around December last year, when Compaq announced the Tru64
Enthusiast licence they did so with a bunch of fanfare about
how this would benefit educational institutions. Some of us
questioned that assertion as the terms and conditions appeared
to specifically preclude use in an educational (classroom)
setting although some Compaq folks said they thought
educational use was intended to be OK.

 Checking the enthusiast web page again today it appears
all mention of educational institutions has been removed
and some language specifically excluding any "institutional"
usage has been added to the terms and conditions.

  OTOH there have been recent postings that a very highly
placed Compaq official has said they will be offering free
VMS licenses to educational institutions. This appears to
be a very mixed message ( preclude us from using cheap
Tru64 but offer free VMS ).

  This is more than a moot point. We're planning a new computer
lab and debating things like X Terms vs PCs running Linux. It
appears I could pitch a Tru64 lab running on PWS 500s ( which
can be had pretty cheaply on the used market ), but not if
I have to pay $1000/seat for the Tru64 licenses. If anyone
knows of any plans to offer free Tru64 ( or make the
entusiast progam available for this sort of usage ) I'd
certainly appreciate hearing about it.

  Of course such a lab could also run VMS should the rumoured
free licenses ever come through ;-)




