Yeah, that's what I thought, too.  Until I put my money down, installed
the software, and crashed my Alpha.  Over and over again.  "Yeah, we've
heard of problems like that, but since we can't reproduce them, they
don't matter to us." was the response.

I got my money back, and then sent it to Micro-Magic.  Not all of it --
it was $10 cheaper than CdrWin.

They make CD Composer that is Alpha native, too.  Doing data disks is a
bit of an exercise (you've got to use mkisofs to build your CD image
first, then CDComposer works with that).  But music CD's are a breeze.
The program will even make MP3's from your existing CD's while cross-
referencing CD & track info off the CDDB on the Internet.

 http://www.cdcomposer.com/

Free eval there, too.

I'd recommend a SCSI CD-R; I use a Panasonic 7503, 8x20, that I picked
up on the net for about $130.  Great device.

