> :I would like to dial up my old VAX which has a DHV11. I have a
> :9600 baud modem connected to one of the ports on the DHV11. Each
> :time I try to dail in it comes back with the error Your VAX/VMS
> :modem is wired wrong please see your system manager.

Have your seen your system manager ? :-)

I used to get that a lot in previous versions of VMS, but I beleive that at
5.5-2, the messages disapeared. What version of VMS do you have ?

Are you able to SET HOST/DTE TXAn: and hang on for more than 30 seconds
without getting a "hangup" message displayed ?

Also, if you dial into the VAX, log in succesfully, but then pull the phone
plug, does your process continue, or does the process get killed (eg: does
your modem signal loss of carrier to the vax ?).  

The IO USers's Manual section on the terminal driver has a page that shows the
logic used for modem signals. 

Getting to know your modem and VMS intimately takes about half to a full day
to ensure both work properly (flow control, security, and handling both
inbound and outbound calls).

Also, make sure your modem provides no feedback for inbound calls.  Not all
modems are capable of this. (eg: modem should not send "RING", "ANSWER"
"CONNECT" text to the VAX when a call comes in.  The first thing VMS needs to
see is the <CR> sent by the remote user.



