>so, what model numbers (or third party units) do I need to be
>looking out for? Are these things high-maintenance as I imagine
>or do they just keep working year after year?
	I don't have a PDP or VAX just a Rainbow 100 and a Vt180
computer/terminal from DEC but the drives you are talking about came
in two varieties. both are 9 track drives. the two types that I know
of are (slow) and (fast) the fast drives use a vacumme chamber to
lower the amount of resistance of the tape path (they have a vacumme
pump inside). the other type works more like an audio Open Reel
recorder. These types work just like the Audio version. you thread the
tape through the heads and the caspins. Btw both types (especially the
slow ones) can be autoload or Manual load. I saw one of those high
speed dudes load up on a IBM mainframe at college. COOL!
	I don't know if they use a proprietary interface or something
close to QIC-02 or QIC-36. I strongly doubt SCSI however.
	Perhaps a tape controller board is one of the pieces you need.
(and BTW, I would like one of those drives and a SCSI adaptor for it
myself), however I really don't have the room for one.

