Dominique:

It sounds a little like a SCSI address problem, or may be a flaky disk drive.
Make sure that each SCSI device has it's own unique SCSI address.  Typically (in
the DEC world) the HD's are 0,1,2(and sometimes 3), a CD is 4, and a tape drive
is 5. Also, the DEC RZ series of HD's have a jumper for spin up on power up
versus spin up on system call, this might be a source of problems on your Mac.

Good luck

Tom Crabtree
tccrab@sunset.net



