Compaq Enterprise Technical Symposium 2000 - CETS2000

Seminar Call For Participation

Potential speakers are invited to submit proposals for pre-conference
seminars!

Pre-Conference Seminars - Scheduled for Sunday, October 1 and Monday,
October 2, the pre-conference seminars may be either one or two days in
length. These seminars are a separate fee from the main conference.

Event Overview:
-----------------

CETS2000 is scheduled for October 1-6, 2000 in Los Angeles at the Los
Angeles Convention Center. In addition, there will be two days of technical
seminars on the Sunday and Monday just prior to the start of the conference.
A technical audience of approximately 4,000 people is expected to attend,
comprised mainly of IT professionals who design, develop, implement,
integrate, maintain, support and/or install solutions in the Compaq style of
computing. Prominent audiences at this event include:

- Compaq customers, including those in Compaq technical user group
communities such as DECUS

- Compaq Accredited Systems Engineers (Master ASEs, ASEs, Associate ASEs)

- Compaq solution partners, such as value-added resellers, application
developers, systems integrators, consultants, ISPs and ASPs

- Compaq technical pre-sales and field employees

See http://www.decus.org/CETS2000/CETS2000_Teaser.shtml for initial details

Guidelines:
-----------

These are strictly technical seminars
NO sales or marketing pitches
In-depth technical information designed to help attendees solve problems
Demonstrations of the technology
Real-life experiences or case studies

Submission Procedures:
------------------------

Send Email to TrishG@CETS2000.com for details

Awards:
---------

Each scheduled seminar speaker will receive a full conference registration
($1395 value), 2 nights hotel logging, domestic discount air fare, and
meals.  In addition if you are scheduled to present two seminars there will
an additional hotel night awarded.








