:Im a young UNIX-freak, who has become a bit interested in the VMS
:operating system :-). So, i want a VAX and i have been offered some used
:VAXen:
:
:Digital VAXstation 3100/M76 - SPX
:Digital VAXstation 4000 - 60
:Digital VAXserver 3100 (Scsi disk Ext. SCSI udtag)

  Of those three systems, the VAXstation 4000 model 60 is likely the 
  best choice.  Faster, capable of more memory, and capable of supporting 
  a SCSI system disk above 1.073 GB.    It can optionally have some I/O 
  expansion via an (optional) TURBOchannel bus, as well -- the other 
  systems have very limited expansion.  Next choice would probably be 
  the VAXstation 3100 model 76, though there are a few VAXserver 3100 
  series systems that can be fairly fast boxes -- we need the model 
  number of the system to be sure.  The SPX was the fastest graphics in 
  that VAXstation series, though it's an antique with antique performance
  by current standards.

  All VAXstation 3100 series systems are limited to a system disk
  capacity of 1.073 GB or less.  See the OpenVMS FAQ for details.

  Make sure you have as much memory as you can get -- the VAXstation
  3100 model 76 tops out at 32 MB.  The VAXstation 4000 model 60
  supports rather more.

:and a Digital Storage Expansion (99 MB Disk + CD-ROM)

  The disk is way too small, but the CD-ROM drive will be useful.
  You'll probably want to scrounge a

