Alan.J.Thackray (alant@aethos.co.uk) wrote:
: My Q-LOGIC QLA-1040 UW-Scsi adapter cannot be booted from SRM console,
: on my PC64 system. 

[...]

: Is there a  difference between my QLA-1040, and a genuine DEC KZPBA ??

Yes and no. There is no *technical* difference. However, only certain
revisions of QLA1040 were re-badged as KZPBA - and, for some reason,
SRM checks for these revisions, and will not attempt to load card's
firmware unless the minor revisions match. The card can still be made
to work under Tru64 (at least, under the 4.0 branch) - but you won't
be able to boot from it with standard SRM.

Cheers,

/Serge.P

