:Does anyone know if there is newer firmware than this for the
:VS3100m76 (KA43)? ...
:The one thing I'd really like to have is an EXAMINE/INSTRUCTION 
:console command.

  You'll need an entire system upgrade, then -- AFAIK, the command set 
  on the older VAX systems was never upgraded.  (And if there were a
  newer command set, there'd almost certainly be a version of the ROMs 
  that supported larger system disks -- and there isn't.  Some of the
  VAX systems do have writeable console storage -- as does Alpha -- but 
  the VAXstation 3100 series is not among these systems.)

  I'm assuming you are aware of XDELTA and similar debugging tools, 
  though you do not mention an operating system.  (XDELTA is one of
  the debuggers available with OpenVMS.)

