:serial connection.

  The (non-PC) DB9 and MMJ pinouts are in the OpenVMS FAQ, as are 
  pointers to information on various adapters.

  Keyboard pinout is just the tip of the problem when attempting to
  connect a PC keyboard -- a keyboard other than the LK201 or LK401 
  or LK402 -- into the DEC 3000 series keyboard connector.  You need 
  to deal with the differences in the signaling and protocol.

  The keyboard and mouse protocol for these older systems is in the
  back of the VCB02 documentation -- I've posted another reply on
  a similar topic within the last week or so, with the part number
  and name of the VCB02 techical manual.  (It's 50+ pages of text
  and pictures, more than I can easily provide here -- if I even 
  had a softcopy of it handy, and I don't.)

