Funny that you mention XDELTA, actually...  I went poking around in the
firmware of a KA650 a while back and found the XDELTA code that the
firmware VMB loads for you if you request it.  The interesting thing
is that this version of XDELTA didn't support disassembling instructions,
even though the console command language did.  I've toyed with the idea
of hacking this XDELTA to call the main console code's disassembler, but 
never got the chance (or convenient enough access to an EPROM burner)
to do it.

Does the XDELTA in the KA43 firmware happen to support instruction mode,
by any chance?  (I haven't got images of it's EPROMs yet, nor the tech
manual, so I can't find out for myself...)  If so, maybe the console
command interpreter code could be hacked to call into the XDELTA
disassembler...  Of maybe cut and paste the code from the KA650.

