I was faced with the same problem when my cat Bucky camped on the VR290 I got
from you.  He blocked the air vents and it overheated.  :^(

I bought a 19" Iiyama Visionmaster 450.  It has separate BNCs (as well as a
VGA connector), and does sync-on-green, composite, and separate H/V sync.  It
works great as a replacement for VR290/299s on VS3100 or uVII/GPX machines, as
well as for VRT19-HAs on DECstations or DEC 3000s.  It also works with Sun
SPARC or IBM RS/6000 systems.  I have not found anything it will not sync up
to, actually.

Of course a VR290 is closer to a 21" monitor in PC-speak, so I lost a little
screen real estate, but after seeing the amazing sharpness of the Iiyama, I
did not mind a bit.

They run anywhere from $450 to $500 on the net these days.  It is the only
monitor on my desk these days; I just switch inputs when I move from the VAX
to the Alpha or the Linux box.

The other monitor that looked attractive at the time was the Viewsonic PS790,
but I think recent models have lost the BNC connectors.

