Tom Sevy wrote:
> 
> Does anyone know if Tru64 will run on the Personal Workstation 433a?  This
> system was originally marketed with NT workstation on it.

It will run fine, but you will need the following:

1) Firmware update, you need the firmware for the 433au variant machine.

2) A supported scsi controller. I used a Dec KZPBA which worked fine. The 433a
may or may not have a SCSI controller on board. Early ones don't while i'm told
later ones do.

3) A supported pci video card. A Dec 3D30 (> 30 Xmarks) is probably the best
choice unless you want to do fast 3D work, but look at the SPD for latest on
this.

Regards, Chris



