Folks:

I recently purchased a used graphics adapter for my old Alpha 3000-300X
workstation.  Got a great deal on it, but no documentation.  It
identifies itself (when queried by the console ROM) as:

  DEC PMAG-DA V5.3g (PMAGB-EA : PXG+ D=24, Z=24)

I gather that it's a 24-bit smart frame buffer with Z-buffer memory.

It properly outputs console video, but I'm having some difficulty
getting Digital UNIX 4.0E to recognize it as a graphics device.  My DU
docs don't reference this card specifically, though they mention support
for several close variations.  When it boots, DU complains that the
"PMAG-DA " device isn't present in the tc_options table, which I've
verified to be true.  Unfortunately, rebuilding the kernel isn't causing
the device to be autodetected and added to the table.  I cobbled up a
tc_options entry by hand, mostly guessing at its contents, and got that
warning to go away.  I never did get the X server to recognize it,
though, despite some useless and probably unwise fiddling with
Xserver.conf.

Finally gave up, pulled the card, and backed-out my changes.  I'm not
ready to admit defeat, though.  Can anyone provide advice on how to
configure DU 4.0E to fully recognize this thing?

-jch



