Welcome.  I am running NT Server 4/SP6a on my Multia/UDB doing file-
print (for Mac and Win32 clients) and FTP and SQL-Server 7 for my mini
network.  All in 64mb RAM.  So you *can* do something with the
box.  :)  However, you are probably wasting your time with 3.5,
especially if you are going to use it as a workstation; 3.5/3.51 both
ran video in User Mode, so display is much slower than 4.0 - and the
Multia's TGA video is so slow anyway, you'd really be killing
yourself.  The slow video is the #1 reason (IMHO) that Multia's make
great servers: they fit on your bookshelf, make no noise, and can still
run a modern OS.

At any rate, get your hands on NT4 and you will get the video (and the
rest of the hardware?) autodetected by the NT4 setup.  And it will all
run faster.  I also saw a big difference in performance with the 64mb I
have now compared to the 32 I used to have.


