I have seen other SCSI widgets (exabyte and DAT drives spring to mind)
connected between a host and a BA350 in the past. This on 3000-400 AXP's
running VMS and OSF, and also Vaxstation 3100 M76's. I didn't like the
solution
at all, not only do you have to make sure you don't put anything in the
BA350 slot
corresponding to the SCSI address of the external widget, but also the SCSI
bus
length is getting marginal.

If you put the non-Storageworks unit BETWEEN the host and the BA350, at
least
you can use the internal termination on the BA350, which is how they are
usually configured.

