>Don't know about head status, transport seems to work well (slow load,
>fast wind, slow wind with head going full up).
>Was it really possible to format a TK50 as a TK70?
>And if it was, how can I reformat them as TK50?

Yes, it is possible to format a TK50 cartridge in a TK70 to the TK70
format if the tape was first degaussed with a bulk tape eraser.  They
are not as reliable as a TK52 or CompacTape II cartridge at the higher
data density.  To go back to TK50 format, just bulk erase it again.
The drive will write new tracks on the tape.  It is also possible that
you could have a bad cartridge.  There used to be a FAQ that listed
the serial number information for a number of bad batches of TK50
cartridges released early on.

